      "reply": "No—these are usually two different ways to get your Medicare coverage, not two policies you buy together. In simple terms, you generally choose one path: Original Medicare means Part A and Part B through the federal program, and Medicare Advantage is a private plan that provides your Part A and Part B instead; if you choose Original Medicare, you can add a separate drug plan and possibly Medigap, but Medigap does not go with Medicare Advantage.",
